## 7. Final Verdict

| Question | Answer |
|---|---|
| Is software development dying? | No. It's transforming. Code-writing is being commoditized; system design is appreciating. |
| Is the "Systems Architect" positioning correct? | Yes. It's the exact role every major expert identifies as AI-proof. |
| Is a case study portfolio better than a code portfolio? | Yes. Unambiguously, across every source. |
| Is the Architect's Theatre the right strategy? | **Yes.** It's not just right — it's ahead of where most developers will be in 2-3 years. |
| What's the risk? | Not launching. The strategy is sound. Execution is the variable. |

> **Kent Beck said it best: "AI won't replace software engineers, but it will expose the ones who never learned to think like engineers."**
>
> The Architect's Theatre is designed to prove you think like an engineer. Ship it.

